                    <occupation>Writer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>See Ed Pope: 27.10.1788 Swift at Miss Williams' / 12.2.1790 again.
                            Theophilus Swift DNB 1746-1815. See Letters of Anna Seward, ii 129, 285.
                            Although Anna Seward doesn't appear in Godwin's diary she was close to H
                            M Williams and introduced her friends to her, see Weston, Penelope
                            Sophia and Powell, Jane. According to the DNB Swift lived in Dublin but
                            his Female Parliament is prefaced 41 Wigmore St 1.5.1789, and he fought
                            a duel with Colonel Lennox on the Uxbridge Road on 3.7.1789 </p>
